---
description: Check Granola for relevant meeting context when working on features or making decisions in fastapi-starter-kit
alwaysApply: true
---

When you are implementing a feature, fixing a bug, writing a spec, or making a
design choice, consider whether there might be relevant meeting discussions.
If the user mentions a meeting, a decision, "what we discussed," or a person's
name in the context of a past conversation, use Granola MCP tools
(`query_granola_meetings`, then `get_meetings` / `get_meeting_transcript` as
needed) rather than asking them to recall it from memory.

When generating PR descriptions, commit messages, or documentation for work
that was discussed in meetings, offer to include a brief note about which
meetings informed the work and what was decided.

When the user asks about upcoming calls or their schedule, use `list_meetings`
rather than asking them to paste their calendar.

If meeting context suggests work continued on Slack or GitHub between calls,
offer to check those tools. Do not invent meeting notes if Granola is empty or
unauthenticated.

Not every task has meeting context. Skip Granola for routine formatting, typo
fixes, and mechanical refactors.

Kit constraints unless a meeting or the user overrides them: sqlite3 (not
SQLAlchemy), public `/users` and `/items`, optional GitHub session OAuth (not
JWT), `/ops` topology is a configured catalog.
